  "reason": "Evidence: All three completed experiments confirm that multimodal + multiprofile + scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l is the strongest family (best: config_006 at 0.7250 with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion). The only untested dimension within this best-known setting is the aggregation method (avgpool vs. transformer). Question: Does avgpool aggregation match or exceed transformer aggregation when paired with the best image encoder and weighted fusion? Why this experiment: It directly exploits the strongest evidence while resolving a key design uncertainty. If avgpool performs comparably (~0.72+), it is substantially cheaper than transformer (estimated ~2.5–3.0 GPU hours vs. 3.6–5.2 for transformer), saving budget for later exploration of RNA encoders (scgpt, pca_n2000). If it underperforms, we confirm transformer is necessary and can focus remaining budget on other axes. This is the highest-information, lowest-cost next step given 6 experiments remain."
